From: Herman van Hazendonk <github.com@herrie.org>
Subject: [PATCH] halium: leave charger-mode boots to the distro

identify_boot_mode() turns androidboot.mode=charger, and MediaTek's
boot_mode 8 and 9, into BOOT_MODE=android, and mountroot() then switches
root to the Android image's own init for its charger UI.

A distro image cannot run that. On LuneOS the BlackBerry KEY2 sat on the
bootloader logo for as long as it was plugged in, and on a device whose
Android image does start the charger, it takes DRM master and keeps the
compositor from ever getting it. Upstream Halium dropped this for Android
8+ in 2021 for the same reason ("Charging is to be handled by rootfs",
halium_no_avoid_android_mode).

LuneOS's init.sh now decides what a charger boot shows before it calls
mountroot (luneos-charger, run from the initramfs), so by the time this
runs the answer is always "boot LuneOS". Keep only the factory and meta
modes (boot_mode 1 and 4) going to Android.

Signed-off-by: Herman van Hazendonk <github.com@herrie.org>
Upstream-Status: Inappropriate [LuneOS-specific: init.sh handles charger boots before mountroot]
---
 scripts/halium | 14 ++++++++++----
 1 file changed, 10 insertions(+), 4 deletions(-)

diff --git a/scripts/halium b/scripts/halium
index f75f344..15c88d7 100644
--- a/scripts/halium
+++ b/scripts/halium
@@ -39,8 +39,14 @@ identify_boot_mode() {
 		esac
 	done
 
-	if echo "$android_bootmode" | grep charger; then
-		BOOT_MODE="android"
+	# A charger-mode boot is NOT handed to Android's init here. The distro's
+	# init decides what a charger boot shows before mountroot is called (on
+	# LuneOS: luneos-charger, from the initramfs), and by the time it gets
+	# this far the answer is "boot the distro". Android's own charger UI
+	# cannot run from a distro image, and upstream Halium stopped doing this
+	# for Android 8+ too ("Charging is to be handled by rootfs").
+	if echo "$android_bootmode" | grep -q charger; then
+		tell_kmsg "charger-mode boot: left to the distro, booting it"
 	fi
 
 	## Some devices may be using 'bootreason', others 'boot_reason'
@@ -52,8 +58,8 @@ identify_boot_mode() {
 		case "${boot_reason}" in
 		1) BOOT_MODE="android" ;; # Meta
 		4) BOOT_MODE="android" ;; # Factory
-		8) BOOT_MODE="android" ;; # Power off charging
-		9) BOOT_MODE="android" ;; # Low power charging
+		# 8 (power-off charging) and 9 (low-power charging) are charger
+		# boots, left to the distro as above.
 		esac
 	fi
 
